    33["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Room Service</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Software System]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Lets friends play one world<br />together (server/): a<br />Cloudflare Worker that makes<br />rooms and a Durable Object<br />per shared world that keeps<br />the world and each player's<br />progress, checks every<br />message, and relays positions<br />and edits between up to 100<br />players. The moderator can<br />make a copy of a world to<br />play as one of its players<br />(server/src/copy.js), apart<br />from the real one, download a<br />whole world as a backup file<br />and put a world that's gone<br />back from one<br />(server/src/backup.js), and<br />has a page listing every<br />world's players, sortable by<br />progress<br />(server/src/admin.js). See<br />server/README.md for the<br />rules and security limits.</div>"]
